{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for the proposed R3 revision 23 design at exact d2639ad944ed265ffac267f1d61f5dc3350cf5d2. One new P2 remains. This is evidence-only ordinary design review, not implementation closure, adoption, landing or source acceptance.\n\nP2 — Require the installation's declared exception, not just one controller (main note 7790–7799, 7911–7955 and missing form 11 at 8016). I freshly inspected the actual effective planner assertion 19cd4a03c32d29a83c9a553112b57f4fec8d8bac, resting directly on 4a1c97f2 and 42de9e34. It permits an installation with one controller to declare a stated exception in its rules. The candidate instead says the exception holds when exactly one active member with an active key holds rules.publish at the observed membership head, and then that member's signed merge meets the rules extent. Neither the proposed Extent fields nor the exception judgment requires a declared opt-in in the repository's observed rules. Thus after missing observation form 11 is built, a repository that never declared the exception can have its author's own rules change reserved solely because its controller count has fallen to one. Recording the exception in the reservation, lane reason and receipt proves it was used; it does not establish permission to use it. Repair the design by requiring an explicit declaration in the rules judged at reservation, with absence meaning unavailable, and bind the recorded exception to that observed rules revision as well as the membership head. Name any unbuilt declaration form and its owner. Keep the ordinary independent-controller bar, the default ban on author review, the remaining extents and checks, and the single-controller exception that the planner actually authorized. This is a future design authorization defect; form 11 currently prevents judging any exception. No present runtime bypass or deployed incident is asserted.\n\nThe previous P2 in verdict 6f9cc0c7 is repaired at design level. Main row 8260 and 9123–9187 atomically open a root-changing operation and its save, refuse another such intend for the entire open-save interval (before or after freezing), refuse the ninth unsaved attempt before admission, and require every unsaved root-changing attempt of the registered instance in a cut. Failed closures retain their attempts; a stop or person can save all eight. No partial cut marks a dirty root saved or ends a host. The six-case table at 9193–9215 supplies one retry/stop successor and preserves three tries, exact attempt identity, prior/checkpoint/journals, unknown ownership and final-cut custody. Producer script counts are attributed evidence, not checker execution. The recovery and IA owners are asked for these admission and whole-set rules; their agreement or implementation is not inferred. Fresh delegated bounded reading of adopted C2 confirms serialization, but its selected-set bound alone is not whole-root proof.\n\nArchitecture: the save repair fits one open save and one frozen cut place, while keeping checkpoint, entry, byte and unknown-operation duties separate. Deployment/authority class requirements now name branch destination custody, grant and replayable records; external effect destinations remain missing form 12. Approvers remain grants in membership; single-member grants remain missing form 13. R2's fdc3d7e2 successor owns lane reading and both digest changes. Thirteen missing forms comprise three decision answers and ten owed forms; the symlink-target gap remains explicitly open. Do not replace those forms, the source witnesses or complete product scope with this review.\n\nSecurity: the planner permits a declared exception, which needs an explicit policy check in addition to the fresh controller count. Count observations and three recorded histories are useful but not substitutes for that check. Existing custody, no credential exposure, local authority windows, author/controller distinctions, observed reservation authority, held unknown writes, effect versus attempt settlement, pins and recovery survive. No rule-count implementation or real provider/device witness is accepted.\n\nSimplification: keep the bounded atomic admission repair. A single explicit optional exception declaration, checked under the rules that the destination already observes, preserves configurable repository policy without an implicit membership-derived policy change. Missing declaration means the exception cannot be used. No separate approval system or new lifecycle is requested.\n\nBreadth and value: retain all six I3 platform definitions, the separate IA task runtime, browser/CLI/MCP/device paths, holds/forks/pins, replay, gateway attempts, reservation/readback/receipt/operator duties, all five composed capacity dimensions under cc570, extents under 42de9e34, C1–C4 and full recovery witnesses, E1 settlement/removal, cold setup/edit-review economics and the complete product acceptance stories. Milestone F is not M1 or full I3 acceptance. The recorded R1 revision 18 adoption 64100829 and demo plan 019 direction 8b626625 are later basis news: optional assignment, membership comments, recorded closes-on-merge, split/recombine, narrow agent refusal and customizable rules remain follow-through obligations. No time estimate narrows scope.\n\nEvidence: exact current three artifacts and producer/request chain were safely inspected; primary first. Prepare confirmed evidence-only, zero implementation closures and not mergeable. Seven fresh delegated partitions cover all current main lines 1–10517, corrections characters 0–260180 and the complete facts ledger: 1,310,661 B / 13,892 LF, with no old-body transfer or personal whole-main claim by a partial reader. Root read the complete fresh native U3 (59,099 B / 602 LF, SHA256 061c1aef88f468aefc4c4b03a3c8cea8fb88ebac4e99bb3fb0d9ef232f480877), all seven reports through EOF, qualified suffix attribution and targeted current extent/save contexts. Native blobs, byte counts and hashes match; all six raw sealed partitions match exact immutable Git and the final suffix hash matches its exact native range. The planner decision was verified by root, not merely the companion reader's attribution. Historical fact-ledger source and witness claims stay dated.\n\nNonblocking: qualify the final witness catalogue's R1 revision 15 draft citation at 10512 and dated sibling status against newer adopted R1 revision 18 / C2 revision 9. These do not reopen historical adoption or imply source correctness.\n\nTesting and limits: current working-tree docs/testing.md was read in full. Native trees are prior ccf974742d998cda56c0e57f9fe8a828adfba7e4 and candidate d395258a985b68de78342bceb40071b3b5676dee; only the main note and corrections changed, with no source or test changes. No tests, gate, build, install, project scripts, repository imports, private diagnostics, evaluator/protocol simulation, provider work or source edits were performed. This verdict gives static design evidence and no gate certification. The existing private-diagnostic restriction was retained, not retried through another path. Root evidence ledger: /tmp/artroom-checker-r3d263-ordinary-root-binding.json.\nHead-news disposition: freshly read exact 16ad9e9f, 4659cbb1 and own locator request 7b1866d8 in full safe projection. Preserve the planner's existing-owner join: fdc3d7e2 requires every extent obligation met and reserved before admitted merge, whereas candidate 8039–8044 permits a lane admission on stale local rules and later destination refusal. That early judgment is not delivery of the stronger successor condition; R2/R3 must define pending versus admitted versus reserved, retain the duty across rule changes, or obtain an explicit amendment. No silent weakening or successor source acceptance is credited. Adopted recovery revision 9 reconciliation, exception observation/records and full five-dimensional capacity remain owed. Builder locator d70b7d9f supplied the existing planner policy identity; root verified it directly.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:11e239eb867f98a198043f61acb3fcbb92b2cacb","binding":"evidence-only","head":"d2639ad944ed265ffac267f1d61f5dc3350cf5d2","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:16ad9e9f63e9bf454a4766306ab6548b52fc79bb\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4659cbb1e19241a903b7272b58b950f064fec988\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:46fe60ca1415634e640fb87fdd0d82f2e367184a\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7b1866d8be9deb759a889b0954a3289a2a659ef6\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d70b7d9fe5807c2b6c84b02fd1a6582f7d422013","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}